  "worked_solution": "To find a basis of $\\text{Null}(A),$ we need to solve the equation $Ax=0$ and express the solution as a linear combination of linearly independent vectors. Those vectors form a basis of $\\text{Null}(A).$\n\nThe given matrix is already in row echelon form. So, the equation $Ax=0$ corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis implies that the only solution of $Ax=0$ is $x=0.$ So, $\\text{Null}(A)={0},$ which means that the basis of $\\text{Null}(A)$ is the empty set, i.e., $B={\\,}.$",
